Phoenix-RTOS: wire the phoenix audio driver into the build.

Adds the phoenix audio driver (src/audio/phoenix/, copied into the tree by the
port's p_prepare overlay step) to the PHOENIX cmake branch. It is a pull-model
SDL audio backend over the rpi4-audio device node /dev/audio0: SDL's audio thread
fills the mixing buffer via the app callback, then PlayDevice write()s it to
/dev/audio0. That device is PIO with a fixed native format (44100 Hz, stereo,
signed 16-bit LE); its blocking write drains the PWM FIFO at the playback rate,
so it supplies the backpressure and WaitDevice is a no-op. OpenDevice forces the
device spec to that native format and lets SDL build a conversion stream from the
app's requested spec.

SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_PHOENIX gates the driver sources + the SDL_config.h define + the
bootstrap-table entry (placed first, so it is auto-selected ahead of the dummy
driver; every host audio backend is compiled out on Phoenix). Unlike the video
driver this driver is fully self-contained: it needs no out-of-tree glue and
pulls no non-zlib dependency into libSDL2.a.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-08-05 00:26:59.879996589 +0200
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-08-05 00:35:33.049006273 +0200
@@ -1491,6 +1491,20 @@
     set(HAVE_SDL_VIDEO TRUE)
   endif()
 
+  # Phoenix-RTOS audio driver (SDL2 port plan phase 1, step 5). A pull-model
+  # backend over the rpi4-audio device node /dev/audio0: SDL's audio thread fills
+  # the mixing buffer via the app callback, then PlayDevice write()s it to
+  # /dev/audio0. That device is PIO with a fixed native format (44100 Hz, stereo,
+  # signed 16-bit LE); its blocking write drains the PWM FIFO at the playback rate
+  # and provides the backpressure, so WaitDevice is a no-op. Pure zlib, no external
+  # link dependency (unlike the video driver it needs no out-of-tree glue).
+  if(SDL_AUDIO)
+    set(SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_PHOENIX 1)
+    file(GLOB AUDIO_PHOENIX_SOURCES ${SDL2_SOURCE_DIR}/src/audio/phoenix/*.c)
+    list(APPEND SOURCE_FILES ${AUDIO_PHOENIX_SOURCES})
+    set(HAVE_SDL_AUDIO TRUE)
+  endif()
+
 elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT RISCOS AND NOT HAIKU)
   if(SDL_AUDIO)
     if(SYSV5 OR SOLARIS OR HPUX)
